-- src:1944 | (3) In the event of any dispute, the Commissioner has power to
-- src:1945 | decide whether or not the employer is justified in calling upon the
-- src:1946 | employee to work in the circumstances specified in subsection (2)(f).
@ref s 38(3) (src:1944-1946)
GIVEN `there is a dispute about whether the employer is justified in calling upon the employee to work in the circumstances specified in subsection (2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(3) the Commissioner has power to decide whether the employer is justified` MEANS
    IF `there is a dispute about whether the employer is justified in calling upon the employee to work in the circumstances specified in subsection (2)(f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of any dispute" -- "In the event of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled: fork F-EVENT); ruled 2026-11-05 (b)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The least payment for extra work worked at the employer's request.  The hours of "extra work"
-- are the keel's overtime, taken as an input (the keel's function is given the limits above).
-- src:1948 | (4) If an employee at the request of the employer works —
-- src:1950 | (a) more than 8 hours in one day except as provided in
-- src:1951 | paragraphs (d) and (e) of the proviso to subsection (1), or
-- src:1952 | more than 9 hours in one day in any case specified in those
-- src:1953 | paragraphs; or
-- src:1955 | (b) more than 44 hours in one week except as provided in
-- src:1956 | paragraph (f) of the proviso to subsection (1), or more than
-- src:1957 | 48 hours in any one week or more than 88 hours in any
-- src:1958 | continuous period of 2 weeks in any case specified in that
-- src:1959 | paragraph,
-- src:1961 | the employee must be paid for the extra work at the rate of not less
-- src:1962 | than one and a half times the employee’s hourly basic rate of pay
-- src:1963 | irrespective of the basis on which the employee’s rate of pay is fixed.
@ref s 38(4) (src:1948-1963)
GIVEN `the hours of overtime` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 4 hourly basic rate of pay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the employee works the extra hours at the request of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written order under section 41A(2) directs that the entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an employee at the request of the employer works" the extra hours, and subject to the Commissioner's order under section 41A(2)
        IF NOT `the employee works the extra hours at the request of the employer` THEN NOTHING
        IF `a written order under section 41A(2) directs that the entitlement does not apply` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the hours of overtime`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the hours of overtime are the keel's answer, which takes the limits of Part 4 and may be none
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST hours THEN
                CONSIDER `the answer of sch 4 hourly basic rate of pay`
                -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the hourly basic rate of pay is the Fourth Schedule's answer, which may be none
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST hourly THEN JUST (1.5 TIMES hourly TIMES hours)

