`s 39 this Part prevents the employer from agreeing that the salary be paid by the task` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is that the salary is paid at an agreed rate in accordance with the task, the specific amount of work required to be performed, and not by the day or by the piece`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Part prevents any employer from agreeing with any employee that the employee’s salary be paid at an agreed rate in accordance with the task" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 39 speaks only of an agreement to pay by the task
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 40 Shift workers, etc.`

DECLARE `s 40(2A) Case` IS ONE OF
    `s 40(2A)(a) accident, actual or threatened`
    `s 40(2A)(b) work, the performance of which is essential to the life of the community`
    `s 40(2A)(c) work essential for defence or security`
    `s 40(2A)(d) urgent work to be done to machinery or plant`
    `s 40(2A)(e) an interruption of work which it was impossible to foresee`
    `s 40(2A)(f) work to be performed by employees in any industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore or any of the essential services as defined under Part 3 of the Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955`
    `s 40(2A) some other case`

-- src:2000 | 40.—(1) Despite section 38(1), an employee who is engaged under
-- src:2001 | his or her contract of service in regular shift work or who has
-- src:2002 | otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours
-- src:2003 | of work specified in this section may be required to work more than
-- src:2004 | 6 consecutive hours, more than 8 hours in any one day or more than
-- src:2005 | 44 hours in any one week but the average number of hours worked
-- src:2006 | over any continuous period of 3 weeks must not exceed 44 hours per
-- src:2007 | week.
@ref s 40(1) (src:2000-2007)
GIVEN `the employee is engaged under the contract of service in regular shift work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours of work specified in section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) section 40 applies to the employee` MEANS
    IF `the employee is engaged under the contract of service in regular shift work` OR `the employee has otherwise consented in writing to work in accordance with the hours of work specified in section 40`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employee who is engaged under his or her contract of service in regular shift work or who has otherwise consented in writing"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The limit for "overtime" under section 40: an average of 44 hours a week over any continuous
-- period of 3 weeks.  There is no limit of hours in one day to compare with: the employee "may be
-- required to work ... more than 8 hours in any one day" (subsection (1)), up to 12 (subsection (3)).
@ref s 40(1) (src:2000-2007)
GIVEN `section 40 applies to the employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 40(1) the limit of hours in one week` MEANS
    IF `section 40 applies to the employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 44
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the average of 44 hours is for "an employee who is engaged under his or her contract of service in regular shift work or who has otherwise consented in writing"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 40(1) (src:2000-2007)
GIVEN `the total hours worked over the 3 continuous weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) the average number of hours worked per week over the 3 weeks is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the total hours worked over the 3 continuous weeks` AT MOST (3 TIMES 44)
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the average number of hours worked over any continuous period of 3 weeks must not exceed 44 hours per week" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2009 | (2) No consent given by an employee under this section is valid
