-- src:2044 | day.
@ref s 40(3) (src:2041-2044)
GIVEN `the number of hours the employee works in the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the case is one described in subsection (2A)(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3) the employee may work the hours in the day` MEANS
    IF (`the number of hours the employee works in the day` GREATER THAN 12) AND (NOT `the case is one described in subsection (2A)(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee to whom this section applies must not under any circumstances work for more than 12 hours in any one day" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
