    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 38(4) does not apply to the section 40 employee; instead the hours over an average of
-- 44 a week across 3 continuous weeks are paid for as extra work "in accordance with section 38(4)".
-- src:2048 | (4) Section 38(4) does not apply to any employee to whom this
-- src:2049 | section applies, but any such employee who at the request of his or
-- src:2050 | her employer works more than an average of 44 hours per week over
-- src:2051 | any continuous period of 3 weeks must be paid for the extra work in
-- src:2052 | accordance with section 38(4).
@ref s 40(4) (src:2048-2052)
GIVEN `the total hours worked over the 3 continuous weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 4 hourly basic rate of pay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the employee works the extra hours at the request of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written order under section 41A(2) directs that the entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 40(4) the least payment for the extra work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such employee who at the request of his or her employer works more than an average of 44 hours per week", and subject to the Commissioner's order under section 41A(2)
        IF NOT `the employee works the extra hours at the request of the employer` THEN NOTHING
        IF `a written order under section 41A(2) directs that the entitlement does not apply` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the total hours worked over the 3 continuous weeks` AT MOST (3 TIMES 44) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the answer of sch 4 hourly basic rate of pay`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the hourly basic rate of pay is the Fourth Schedule's answer, which may be none
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST hourly THEN JUST (1.5 TIMES hourly TIMES (`the total hours worked over the 3 continuous weeks` MINUS (3 TIMES 44)))

§§ `s 41 Interpretation of "week" for purposes of sections 36, 38 and 40`

-- "Week" is a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on Sunday.  The week that holds a
-- day is found by stepping back to the Sunday on or before it.
-- src:2056 | 41. In sections 36, 38 and 40, “week” means a continuous period of
-- src:2057 | 7 days commencing at midnight on Sunday.
@ref s 41 (src:2056-2057)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 41 the week that holds the day` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS sunday, `last day` IS sunday PLUS 6
    WHERE
        sunday MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `is a Sunday` day THEN day
                IF `is a Sunday` (day MINUS 1) THEN day MINUS 1
                IF `is a Sunday` (day MINUS 2) THEN day MINUS 2
                IF `is a Sunday` (day MINUS 3) THEN day MINUS 3
                IF `is a Sunday` (day MINUS 4) THEN day MINUS 4
                IF `is a Sunday` (day MINUS 5) THEN day MINUS 5
                OTHERWISE day MINUS 6

§§ `s 41A Power to exempt`

-- src:2061 | 41A.—(1) The Commissioner may, after considering the
-- src:2062 | operational needs of the employer and the health and safety of the
-- src:2063 | employee or class of employees, by written order exempt an
-- src:2064 | employee or any class of employees from sections 38(1), (5) and
-- src:2065 | (8) and 40(3) subject to such conditions as the Commissioner thinks
-- src:2066 | fit.
@ref s 41A(1) (src:2061-2066)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has made a written order after considering the operational needs of the employer and the health and safety of the employee or class of employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order covers the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(1) the employee is exempt from sections 38(1), (5) and (8) and 40(3)` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has made a written order after considering the operational needs of the employer and the health and safety of the employee or class of employees` AND `the order covers the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by written order exempt an employee or any class of employees", after considering the operational needs of the employer and the health and safety of the employee
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Seam S5: the answer asked for by s 88(4) (ea2).
-- src:2068 | (2) The Commissioner may, after considering the operational needs
-- src:2069 | of an employer and the interests of an employee or a class of
-- src:2074 | employees, by written order, direct that the entitlement to be paid for
-- src:2075 | extra work under section 37(2) or (3), 38(4), 40(4) or 88(4) does not
-- src:2076 | apply to that employee or class of employees, subject to such
-- src:2077 | conditions as the Commissioner thinks fit.
@ref s 41A(2) (src:2068-2077)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has made a written order after considering the operational needs of the employer and the interests of the employee or class of employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order covers the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(2) the entitlement to be paid for extra work does not apply to the employee` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has made a written order after considering the operational needs of the employer and the interests of the employee or class of employees` AND `the order covers the employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by written order, direct that the entitlement to be paid for extra work under section 37(2) or (3), 38(4), 40(4) or 88(4) does not apply"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 41A(3) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 41A(3) the employer`

DECLARE `s 41A(3) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 41A(3) display the order or a copy of it conspicuously in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed`

-- src:2079 | (3) Where the Commissioner —
-- src:2081 | (a) exempts an employee or any class of employees from
-- src:2082 | section 38(1), (5) or (8) or 40(3); or
-- src:2084 | (b) directs that the entitlement to be paid for extra work under
-- src:2085 | section 37(2) or (3), 38(4), 40(4) or 88(4) does not apply to
-- src:2086 | an employee or any class of employees,
-- src:2088 | the employer must display the order or a copy thereof conspicuously
-- src:2089 | in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed.
@ref s 41A(3) (src:2079-2089)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has exempted the employee under subsection (1) or directed under subsection (2) that the entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order or a copy of it is displayed conspicuously in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(3) the employer has displayed the order` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has exempted the employee under subsection (1) or directed under subsection (2) that the entitlement does not apply`
    THEN JUST `the order or a copy of it is displayed conspicuously in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Commissioner" exempts or directs
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The duty as a yes/no question (the DEONTIC below carries the same rule): "Where the
-- Commissioner exempts ... or directs ..., the employer must display the order".
@ref s 41A(3) (src:2079-2089)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has exempted the employee under subsection (1) or directed under subsection (2) that the entitlement does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(3) the employer must display the order` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has exempted the employee under subsection (1) or directed under subsection (2) that the entitlement does not apply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioner" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met, the Commissioner has neither exempted nor directed
    ELSE JUST FALSE
-- The duty carries no time: it is held as a rule with no deadline.
@ref s 41A(3) (src:2079-2089)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 41A(3) Actor` `s 41A(3) Action`
`s 41A(3) the employer's duty to display the order` MEANS
    PARTY `s 41A(3) the employer`
    MUST `s 41A(3) display the order or a copy of it conspicuously in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 41A(3) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not display the order or a copy of it conspicuously in the place where the employee or class of employees are employed"
